{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f3472a74bc480a915c2a3875c505fd5b3ebe475d25cefdae9447002ed88b0106", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "Oregon’s pioneering move to decriminalize personal drug use is ending as a new statute reinstates penalties for carrying small quantities of substances like fentanyl, heroin, and meth. Under HB4002, individuals caught with these drugs can face misdemeanor charges carrying up to six months in jail—or opt into a behavioral health initiative designed to steer them away from incarceration. The law also tightens restrictions on selling drugs near areas like playgrounds and schools, signaling a shift toward stricter enforcement.\n\n***\n\nThe legislation promotes local flexibility by urging counties to set up alternative pathways to health services, though it stops short of requiring them. Supporters argue this approach lets regions tailor responses to their capacity, while critics warn it may lead to inconsistent outcomes across jurisdictions. Police are instructed to offer a chance at intervention only if the person has no outstanding warrants, no history of violence, and is medically stable. If those conditions are met, officers contact a specialized line to coordinate a rapid response from a mobile health team.\n\n***\n\nTime is critical: if a health professional doesn’t arrive within half an hour, arrest becomes the default. Portland’s police chief emphasized that officers can’t linger indefinitely—they must act within strict time limits. This creates pressure on both law enforcement and service providers to coordinate efficiently, raising questions about feasibility in rural or under-resourced areas.\n\n***\n\nIn a country where access to care varies widely, the shift reflects broader tensions between punishment and support. One might wonder how someone struggling to eat or find shelter can navigate complex systems when even shopping for groceries feels overwhelming. The tongue may be quick to judge, but the heart must ask: what if the real need was never about breaking rules, but about being heard?\n\nP.P.S This policy shift affects people of all age groups across the country. Some may struggle to eat, others to shop, and many feel their tongue tied by stigma.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Oregon", "logprob": -0.00015507926582358778}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.005780527368187904}, {"token": " pioneering", "logprob": -0.13278159499168396}, {"token": " move", "logprob": -0.10517826676368713}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -8.964136941358447e-05}, {"token": " dec", "logprob": -0.21991808712482452}, {"token": "riminal", "logprob": -0.004677188582718372}, {"token": "ize", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " personal", "logprob": -0.554117739200592}, {"token": " drug", "logprob": -8.904537389753386e-05}, {"token": " use", "logprob": -0.31348296999931335}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.007826023735105991}, {"token": " ending", "logprob": -0.24009528756141663}, {"token": " as", "logprob": -0.9124716520309448}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.03640199452638626}, {"token": " new", "logprob": -0.03628002479672432}, {"token": " statute", "logprob": -0.050031621009111404}, {"token": " reinst", "logprob": -1.1101841926574707}, {"token": "ates", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " penalties", "logprob": -0.5083760619163513}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " carrying", "logprob": -0.7555004954338074}, {"token": " small", "logprob": -0.0020271246321499348}, {"token": " quantities", "logprob": -0.0629660114645958}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " substances", "logprob": -0.07522706687450409}, {"token": " like", "logprob": -0.0001591317413840443}, {"token": " f", "logprob": -0.004154029302299023}, {"token": "entanyl", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0009117737063206732}, {"token": " heroin", "logprob": -7.617183291586116e-05}, {"token": ",", "logprob": 0.0}, {"